            <ArticleTitle>Caecal volvulus in an adolescent African male: a case report and brief review of the literature.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>92</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.11604/pamj.2014.17.92.3946</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Caecal volvulus is an infrequent clinical condition caused by an axial twist of ascending colon, caecum and terminal ileum around the mesenteric pedicle. This article presents the case of a 16-year old African male from Kenya who presented to the emergency department with acute onset right sided lower abdominal pain diagnosed intra-operatively as caecal volvulus. The rare nature of the condition, the need for a high index of suspicion and surgical management are highlighted.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
